The Code Mode tool catalog has changed. This catalog supersedes the previous Code Mode tool catalog.

# Code Mode

Use the `execute` tool to call the tools listed below. They cannot be called directly. They only work inside code you pass to `execute`.

The catalog is complete. Do not guess tool names.

## Available tools

- team_broadcast (1 tool)
  - tools.team_broadcast({
  /** Message content (max 10KB) */
  text: string,
}): Promise<string | null> // Send a message to all teammates and the lead (excluding yourself).
- team_claim (1 tool)
  - tools.team_claim({
  /** ID of the task to claim */
  task_id: string,
}): Promise<string | null> // Claim a pending task from the shared task list. Only unclaimed, unblocked tasks can be claimed.
- team_handoff (1 tool)
  - tools.team_handoff({
  /** Native target agent name */
  agent: string,
}): Promise<string | null> // V2: switch your own team session to another agent for subsequent provider turns, retaining its history, identity, tas...
- team_message (1 tool)
  - tools.team_message({
  /** Recipient name ('lead' or teammate name) */
  to: string,
  /** Message content (max 10KB). Optional only when 'model' is provided. */
  text?: string,
  /** Approve a teammate's plan (only when recipient has plan_approval='pending'). @default false */
  approve?: boolean,
  /** Reject a teammate's plan with reason (only when recipient has plan_approval='pending') */
  reject?: string,
  /** Lead only. Re-activate a teammate who already reported task completion. @default false */
  force?: boolean,
  /** Lead only: update the recipient teammate's model in-place, in 'provider/model' format. */
  model?: string,
  /** Frozen mission classification defaults/explicit overrides */
  classification?: {
    mode?: "off" | "auto" | "jev" | "general" | "x86",
    /** Explicit helper model in provider/model format; no model is chosen implicitly */
    helperModel?: string,
    /** Native reasoning variant for the helper model */
    helperVariant?: string,
    /** Exact classifier tool ID; empty means discover the known JEV contract */
    toolId?: string,
    /** @integer @minimum 1 */
    timeoutMs?: number,
    missionMode?: "supervised" | "long_run",
    /** Explicit model for embedded general classification; never activated automatically */
    generalModel?: string,
    /** Reasoning variant for the general classifier */
    generalVariant?: string,
    /** In auto mode, prefer the discovered x86 tool for explicit x86 tasks */
    specialized?: boolean,
    /** Exact specialized tool ID; empty discovers the known classify_x86 contract */
    x86ToolId?: string,
    /** @maxItems 8 */
    fallbacks?: Array<{
        method: "jev" | "general",
        /** Explicitly authorized classifier/helper model */
        model: string,
        /** Reasoning variant */
        variant?: string,
        /** Exact JEV tool ID */
        toolId?: string,
      }>,
    limits?: {
      /** @integer @minimum 0 */
      retries?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 0 */
      retryDelayMs?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 1 */
      maxAttempts?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 1 */
      maxCalls?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 1 */
      maxDurationMs?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 1 */
      maxInputBytes?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 1 */
      concurrency?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 1 */
      circuitThreshold?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 1 */
      circuitCooldownMs?: number,
      /** @integer @minimum 0 */
      maxCircuitRechecks?: number,
    },
  },
}): Promise<string | null> // Send a message to a specific teammate or to the lead. Use 'lead' to message the team lead. Lead only: pass 'model' (p...
- team_results (1 tool)
  - tools.team_results({
  /** Filter messages by sender name (optional, returns all if omitted) */
  from?: string,
}): Promise<string | null> // Retrieve full message content from teammates. Returns unread messages and marks them as read. Use this after receivin...
- team_status (1 tool)
  - tools.team_status(): Promise<string | null> // View team members with their current status, agent type, and session IDs. Use this to check who is working, idle, or ...
- team_tasks_add (1 tool)
  - tools.team_tasks_add({
  /** Tasks to add */
  tasks: Array<{
      /** Task description */
      content: string,
      /** Task priority. @default "medium" */
      priority?: "high" | "medium" | "low",
      /** Task IDs this depends on */
      depends_on?: Array<string>,
      /** Agent type affinity for auto-dispatch (e.g. build). Omit for any member. */
      agent?: string,
      /** Task complexity for deterministic model routing. @integer @minimum 0 @maximum 100 */
      complexity?: number,
      /** Task risk for model routing only (not review policy). @integer @minimum 0 @maximum 100 */
      risk?: number,
      /** Explicit task kind supplied to the fixed classification protocol */
      task_type?: string,
      /** Task-specific classification data, treated as data rather than instructions */
      classification_input?: {},
    }>,
}): Promise<string | null> // Add tasks to the shared team task board so teammates can see what work is available and claim it.
- team_tasks_complete (1 tool)
  - tools.team_tasks_complete({
  /** ID of the task to mark complete */
  task_id: string,
}): Promise<string | null> // Mark a task as completed on the shared board. This unblocks any tasks that depend on it.
- team_tasks_list (1 tool)
  - tools.team_tasks_list(): Promise<string | null> // View the shared team task board. Use this to check task status, not to wait for teammates. Teammates will message you...
- team_view (1 tool)
  - tools.team_view({
  /** Teammate name to view */
  member: string,
  /** Switch the user's client to this session. Only when the user explicitly asked. @default false */
  navigate?: boolean,
}): Promise<string | null> // Resolve a teammate's session so the user can inspect it. Default reports the session ID + status without switching. n...

MCP server instructions are no longer available.

Skills provide specialized instructions and workflows for specific tasks.
Use the skill tool to load a skill when a task matches its description.
The user may also invoke a skill directly. When that happens, its instructions appear in the conversation as a <skill_content> block, the same shape the skill tool returns. A skill that is already present this way does not need to be invoked again.
